      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To extract table cells and row structure from a document, I can use the Amazon Textract service, which is a machine learning service that automatically extracts text, handwriting, and data from scanned documents. I will import the necessary modules from the boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with the Textract service. I will also include the concrete model identifier or model family in the code to make the provider identifiable. </thinking>\n",
